: none; border-radius: 0; }\n  .cover { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }\n  .badge, .secnum, table.code, .dl { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }\n  h2 { break-after: avoid; }\n  section { break-before: auto; }\n  .card, .evidence, .figure { break-inside: avoid; }\n  a { color: inherit; }\n}\n\n.summary-box { border: 2px solid #0f172a; padding: 8px 14px; margin: 10px 0 14px; }\n.summary-box h3 { margin-top: 6px; }\n.verdict { font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 8px; background-color: #f8fafc; border-left: 4px solid #1d4ed8; }\n.outcome-ok { border-left: 4px solid #15803d; padding: 4px 10px; }\n.outcome-bad { border-left: 4px solid #b91c1c; padding: 4px 10px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n\n<div class=\"cover\">\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">PerfPilot AI \u00b7 Workload optimization experiment</p>\n  <h1>Optimization experiment: Duplicate counter - Count elements once with collections.Counter</h1>\n  <table class=\"cover-meta\">\n    <tr>\n      <td><span class=\"k\">Workload</span><br>duplicate_counter</td>\n      <td><span class=\"k\">Experiment</span><br>optimization</td>\n      <td><span class=\"k\">State</span><br>COMPLETED</td>\n      <td><span class=\"k\">Size</span><br>small</td>\n      <td><span class=\"k\">Generated</span><br>2026-10-20 20:45 UTC</td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p class=\"cover-source\">optimization 0042598d-9a45-4f93-81dc-28ddbbbf6504</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"legend\" id=\"legend\">\n  <h3>How to read this report: provenance labels</h3>\n  <table class=\"data\">\n    <thead><tr><th width=\"20%\">Label</th><th width=\"40%\">Meaning</th><th width=\"40%\">Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><span class=\"legend-term legend-measured\">MEASURED</span></td><td>Produced by running code in an isolated PerfPilot environment.</td><td>A profiler or A/B benchmark result recorded for this audit.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><span class=\"legend-term legend-static\">STATIC</span></td><td>Deterministic AST/rule output. No code was executed.</td><td>A rule matched a pattern at a specific file and line.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><span class=\"legend-term legend-ai_hypothesis\">AI_HYPOTHESIS</span></td><td>LLM- or heuristic-generated suggestion. Unverified until measured.</td><td>A proposed rewrite and its expected (qualitative) effect.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s1\"><span class=\"secnum\">1</span> Outcome: measured vs hypothesis</h2>\n<div class=\"outcome-ok\">\n  <p><strong>Validated and benchmarked: IMPROVED, median speedup 33.13\u00d7 (95% CI [30.13\u00d7, 34.93\u00d7]).</strong> <span class=\"badge status status-completed\">COMPLETED</span></p>\n<ul><li>speedup 33.132x &gt;= 1.053x (5% threshold) and 95% CI [30.134x, 34.929x] excludes 1</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"summary-box\" id=\"measured-vs-hypothesis\">\n  <h3>Measured vs hypothesis</h3>\n  <table class=\"data\">\n    <thead><tr><th width=\"28%\">Measured</th><th width=\"56%\">Value</th><th width=\"16%\">Provenance</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Profiled bottleneck</td><td>count_duplicates (workload.py:10): 99.1% cumulative / 3.3% exclusive of profiled time, 1 call(s) (cProfile, size small)</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Correctness validation</td><td>PASSED: 8/8 required checks passed</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Median wall time</td><td>baseline 1.389 ms -&gt; candidate 0.042 ms (n=8 / 8 timed runs)</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Speedup (median wall-time ratio)</td><td>33.13\u00d7 (95% CI [30.13\u00d7, 34.93\u00d7])</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Latency reduction</td><td>97.0%</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>CPU-time speedup</td><td>34.25\u00d7</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Classification</td><td>IMPROVED at the 5% practical threshold</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>tracemalloc peak (Python allocations, call only)</td><td>baseline 2.5 KiB -&gt; candidate 9.2 KiB (median)</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>RSS peak (sampled, whole child process)</td><td>baseline 26.3 MiB -&gt; candidate 25.9 MiB (median)</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n  <table class=\"data\">\n    <thead><tr><th width=\"28%\">Hypothesis (not measured)</th><th width=\"56%\">Statement</th><th width=\"16%\">Provenance</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Suspected root cause</td><td>`items.count(x)` rescans the whole list on every call. Calling it for every element makes the function O(n^2).</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Expected effect (qualitative)</td><td>Hypothesis: the quadratic rescans disappear (O(n) total), which should dominate for inputs with thousands of items.</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-ai_hypothesis\">AI_HYPOTHESIS</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Estimated impact (qualitative)</td><td>high: complexity change in the function that dominates the profile</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-ai_hypothesis\">AI_HYPOTHESIS</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Memory trade-off</td><td>One dict entry per distinct element.</td><td><span class=\"badge prov prov-ai_hypothesis\">AI_HYPOTHESIS</span></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n  <p class=\"verdict\">Confirmed by measurement: the validated patch is IMPROVED at the 5% practical threshold (speedup 33.13\u00d7, 95% CI [30.13\u00d7, 34.93\u00d7]).</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s2\"><span class=\"secnum\">2</span> Workload &amp; input</h2>\n<table class=\"kv\">\n  <tr><th>Workload</th><td>Duplicate counter (<span class=\"mono\">duplicate_counter</span>) \u00b7 project Bundled examples</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Description</th><td>Count how often each repeated item occurs (list.count called for every element).</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Entrypoint</th><td class=\"mono\">workload:count_duplicates \u00b7 single</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Fixture</th><td><span class=\"mono\">fixtures:make_input</span><br>items: n_items lowercase words drawn from a vocabulary of about unique_ratio*n_items words with Zipf-like frequencies (exponent skew).</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Input size</th><td>small \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">n_items=500</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Input SHA-256</th><td class=\"mono\">2079162d2fcc3377eb667681ca4b1ecb92a1ac116a8039c36077954465f05827<br><span class=\"muted\">benchmark preflight (identical for both variants)</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Expected output</th><td>type: <span class=\"mono\">dict[str, int]</span>; comparison: <span class=\"mono\">exact</span>; rel_tol: <span class=\"mono\">1e-09</span>; abs_tol: <span class=\"mono\">0.0</span>; description: <span class=\"mono\">Mapping of every item that occurs more than once to its occurrence count (dict equality, key order ignored).</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Limits</th><td>timeout 120 s \u00b7 memory 1024 MB</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Registered tree SHA-256</th><td class=\"mono\">ebc38e0a5ea566a0274ff388e478d31347acbc1c8d5e61d6d66e25a543162ffa</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s3\"><span class=\"secnum\">3</span> Environment fingerprint</h2>\n<p><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> <span class=\"muted\">Captured by benchmark run 7e4f1fba-f30a-4243-a54d-68bd3e1f0976.</span></p>\n<table class=\"kv\">\n<tr><th>Captured at</th><td class=\"mono\">2026-10-20T20:45:56.446910+00:00</td></tr><tr><th>PerfPilot version</th><td class=\"mono\">0.1.0</td></tr><tr><th>Python implementation</th><td class=\"mono\">CPython</td></tr><tr><th>Python version</th><td class=\"mono\">3.12.10</td></tr><tr><th>Platform</th><td class=\"mono\">macOS-26.7.1-arm64-arm-64bit</td></tr><tr><th>OS</th><td class=\"mono\">Darwin</td></tr><tr><th>OS release</th><td class=\"mono\">25.6.0</td></tr><tr><th>Architecture</th><td class=\"mono\">arm64</td></tr><tr><th>CPU model</th><td class=\"mono\">Apple M4 Pro</td></tr><tr><th>Logical CPUs</th><td class=\"mono\">14</td></tr><tr><th>Physical CPUs</th><td class=\"mono\">14</td></tr><tr><th>Total memory (bytes)</th><td class=\"mono\">51539607552</td></tr><tr><th>Load average (1/5/15 min)</th><td class=\"mono\">[6.75, 14.99, 10.36]</td></tr><tr><th>uv.lock SHA-256</th><td class=\"mono\">90f60dca8f693889940cba7a3319d493203f9788128d25b7d976af16b85dbfd9</td></tr><tr><th>Packages</th><td class=\"mono\">numpy==2.5.4, psutil==7.2.2, pydantic==2.14.1, sqlalchemy==2.1.4, fastapi==0.143.0, scipy==1.18.1</td></tr></table>\n<p class=\"warning\">thermal state unavailable (not exposed to unprivileged processes)</p><p class=\"warning\">CPU frequency unavailable (not reported, or implausible value from the OS); frequency scaling was not controlled</p><p class=\"warning\">CPU affinity unavailable on this OS; processes were not pinned to a core</p></section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s4\"><span class=\"secnum\">4</span> Profiling evidence</h2>\n<p><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Profile <span class=\"mono\">d9eb8786-9e05-4ee6-b1b3-dc5c2e1511a3</span> \u00b7 SUCCEEDED \u00b7 size small \u00b7 profile used by the analysis that produced this recommendation.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Total profiled time 1.481 ms \u00b7 wall time under the profiler 1.504 ms \u00b7 input SHA-256 <span class=\"mono\">2079162d2fcc3377eb667681ca4b1ecb92a1ac116a8039c36077954465f05827</span></p>\n<table class=\"data\">\n  <thead><tr><th width=\"5%\">#</th><th width=\"33%\">Function</th><th width=\"9%\" class=\"num\">Calls</th><th width=\"13%\" class=\"num\">Exclusive</th><th width=\"10%\" class=\"num\">Excl. %</th><th width=\"13%\" class=\"num\">Cumulative</th><th width=\"10%\" class=\"num\">Cum. %</th><th width=\"7%\">User</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td><span class=\"mono\">&lt;method &#39;count&#39; of &#39;list&#39; objects&gt;</span><br><span class=\"mono loc\">&lt;built-in&gt;:0</span></td><td class=\"num\">500</td><td class=\"num\">1.419 ms</td><td class=\"num\">95.8%</td><td class=\"num\">1.419 ms</td><td class=\"num\">95.8%</td><td>no</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td><span class=\"mono\">count_duplicates</span><br><span class=\"mono loc\">workload.py:10</span></td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">0.048 ms</td><td class=\"num\">3.3%</td><td class=\"num\">1.467 ms</td><td class=\"num\">99.1%</td><td>yes</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td><span class=\"mono\">&lt;method &#39;disable&#39; of &#39;_lsprof.Profiler&#39; objects&gt;</span><br><span class=\"mono loc\">&lt;built-in&gt;:0</span></td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">0.012 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.8%</td><td class=\"num\">0.012 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.8%</td><td>no</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td><span class=\"mono\">call</span><br><span class=\"mono loc\">&lt;harness&gt;/harness_entry.py:215</span></td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">0.002 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.1%</td><td class=\"num\">1.469 ms</td><td class=\"num\">99.2%</td><td>no</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<ul class=\"muted\"><li>Exclusive (pstats tottime): time spent in the function body itself, excluding callees. Exclusive percentages add up to 100% across all functions.</li><li>Cumulative (pstats cumtime): time in the function and everything it called. Cumulative percentages overlap (a caller includes its callees) and are never summed.</li><li>cProfile instruments every call, so absolute profiled times are inflated; use the A/B benchmark for real timings.</li></ul>\n<h3>Memory during the profile (three different quantities)</h3>\n<table class=\"data\">\n  <thead><tr><th width=\"30%\">Metric</th><th width=\"15%\" class=\"num\">Value</th><th width=\"55%\">Definition</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody><tr><td>tracemalloc peak (Python allocations, call only)</td><td class=\"num\">2.5 KiB</td><td>peak Python-traced allocations during one workload call (separate call, input built before tracing). Not process memory.</td></tr><tr><td>RSS peak (sampled, whole child process)</td><td class=\"num\">25.2 MiB</td><td>peak resident set size of the child process tree sampled by the parent over the whole run (interpreter + input + profiled and traced calls)</td></tr><tr><td>ru_maxrss (kernel max RSS, whole child process)</td><td class=\"num\">26.0 MiB</td><td>kernel-reported maximum RSS of the child process (getrusage)</td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"warning\">cProfile adds per-call overhead: absolute times are inflated, and functions with many small calls are over-represented. Use the benchmark for real timings.</p><p class=\"warning\">resource limit RLIMIT_AS not applied: macOS does not enforce RLIMIT_AS/RLIMIT_DATA; memory is bounded by the parent&#39;s sampled-RSS ceiling instead</p></section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s5\"><span class=\"secnum\">5</span> Recommendation</h2>\n<p><strong>Count elements once with collections.Counter</strong> \u00b7 rule <span class=\"mono\">PP-COLL-001</span> \u00b7 rank 1 \u00b7 confidence HIGH \u00b7 generated by deterministic</p>\n<p class=\"mono loc\">workload.py:13 \u00b7 count_duplicates</p>\n<table class=\"kv\">\n  <tr><th>Observed bottleneck <span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></th><td>`count_duplicates` (workload.py:10) accounts for 99.1% of profiled time (cumulative 1.47 ms, exclusive 0.05 ms, 1 call(s)) in profile d9eb8786-9e05-4ee6-b1b3-dc5c2e1511a3 at size small [MEASURED]. Rule PP-COLL-001 flags linear list search/removal inside a loop at workload.py:13 [STATIC].</td></tr>\n<tr><th>Profiler evidence <span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span></th><td>Profile <span class=\"mono\">d9eb8786-9e05-4ee6-b1b3-dc5c2e1511a3</span> (size small): <span class=\"mono\">count_duplicates</span> exclusive 0.048 ms (3.3%), cumulative 1.467 ms (99.1%), 1 call(s).<br><span class=\"muted\">Largest non-workspace functions in the same profile (not attributed to a caller):</span><br><span class=\"mono\">&lt;method &#39;count&#39; of &#39;list&#39; objects&gt;</span>: exclusive 1.419 ms, 500 call(s)</td></tr>  <tr><th>Suspected root cause <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></th><td>`items.count(x)` rescans the whole list on every call. Calling it for every element makes the function O(n^2).</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Proposed optimization <span class=\"badge prov prov-static\">STATIC</span></th><td>Count every element in one pass with `collections.Counter(items)` before the loop and read the count from it.</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Expected effect <span class=\"badge prov prov-ai_hypothesis\">AI_HYPOTHESIS</span></th><td>Hypothesis: the quadratic rescans disappear (O(n) total), which should dominate for inputs with thousands of items.<br><span class=\"muted\">qualitative expectation, not a measurement</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Estimated impact <span class=\"badge prov prov-ai_hypothesis\">AI_HYPOTHESIS</span></th><td>high: complexity change in the function that dominates the profile<br><span class=\"muted\">qualitative expectation, not a measurement</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Correctness risks</th><td><ul><li>Items must be hashable; Counter raises TypeError where list.count() worked.</li><li>Counter matches by hash + ==; list.count() by == only.</li></ul></td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Memory trade-offs <span class=\"badge prov prov-ai_hypothesis\">AI_HYPOTHESIS</span></th><td>One dict entry per distinct element.</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Validation plan</th><td><ol><li>Apply the approved diff to an isolated copy of the workload; verify the original tree hash is unchanged afterwards.</li><li>Run the workload&#39;s tests [&#39;tests&#39;] with pytest in a separate process against the original and the patched copy; at least 10 must pass on both.</li><li>Compare original vs candidate outputs for sizes [&#39;small&#39;, &#39;medium&#39;] x seeds [2024, 7, 11] using exact comparison.</li><li>Compare outputs on 5 contract edge case(s).</li><li>Check exception parity on 2 error input(s).</li><li>Fail if the candidate mutates an input the original leaves untouched.</li><li>Benchmark only after every required check passed.</li></ol></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s6\"><span class=\"secnum\">6</span> Proposed change (diff)</h2>\n<table class=\"kv\">\n  <tr><th>Generated by</th><td>deterministic \u00b7 transform <span class=\"mono\">list_count_to_counter</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Target file</th><td class=\"mono\">workload.py \u00b7 5 changed line(s)</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Original file SHA-256</th><td class=\"mono\">ef703763602064d88b57e5332462aa322b97210968587f9451c4a5aebe13ef83</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Patched file SHA-256</th><td class=\"mono\">fff3db97d8d1a39755bc68cc55035726fc8bca297e67566d163a1163e1b8bafb</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Original tree SHA-256</th><td class=\"mono\">ebc38e0a5ea566a0274ff388e478d31347acbc1c8d5e61d6d66e25a543162ffa</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Patched tree SHA-256</th><td class=\"mono\">1d8241c1da508fbbfd3cad8b9dbbaffd559f60f1ecc89206e0be9965c8ae52af</td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Patch validator</th><td><span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span> \u00b7 parse: passed, paths: passed, protected_files: passed, structure: passed, applies_cleanly: passed, compiles: passed, public_signatures: passed, benchmark_integrity: passed</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>Count every element of `items` once with `Counter(items)` before the loop at line 12 and read counts from it (O(n) total instead of O(n) per call).</p><ul><li>Elements of `items` (and the values counted) must be hashable; otherwise Counter raises TypeError where list.count() worked.</li><li>Counter matches by hash + ==, list.count() by == only; they agree for well-behaved types.</li><li>A missing key reads as 0, exactly like list.count() for an absent value.</li><li>Extra memory: one dict entry per distinct element.</li></ul><div class=\"diff\">\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">--- a/workload.py</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">+++ b/workload.py</div>\n  <div class=\"dl hunk\">@@ -6,11 +6,14 @@</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;from __future__ import annotations</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;</div>\n  <div class=\"dl add\">+from collections import Counter</div>\n  <div class=\"dl add\">+</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;def count_duplicates(items: list[str]) -&gt; dict[str, int]:</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;duplicates: dict[str, int] = {}</div>\n  <div class=\"dl add\">+&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; items_counts = Counter(items)</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for item in items:</div>\n  <div class=\"dl del\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; occurrences = items.count(item)</div>\n  <div class=\"dl add\">+&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; occurrences = items_counts[item]</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if occurrences &gt; 1:</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;duplicates[item] = occurrences</div>\n  <div class=\"dl ctx\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;return duplicates</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s7\"><span class=\"secnum\">7</span> Approval &amp; lifecycle</h2>\n<table class=\"kv\">\n  <tr><th>Approval</th><td><span class=\"badge status status-approved\">APPROVED</span></td></tr>\n  <tr><th>Approved by / at</th><td>local-user \u00b7 2026-10-20 20:45 UTC</td></tr>\n</table>\n<table class=\"data\">\n  <thead><tr><th width=\"22%\">From</th><th width=\"22%\">To</th><th width=\"22%\">At</th><th width=\"34%\">Reason</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody><tr><td>RECOMMENDED</td><td>PATCH_PROPOSED</td><td class=\"mono loc\">2026-10-20T20:45:46.898748Z</td><td>diff proposed by deterministic</td></tr><tr><td>PATCH_PROPOSED</td><td>AWAITING_APPROVAL</td><td class=\"mono loc\">2026-10-20T20:45:46.899609Z</td><td>diff passed the patch validator</td></tr><tr><td>AWAITING_APPROVAL</td><td>AWAITING_APPROVAL</td><td class=\"mono loc\">2026-10-20T20:45:46.925519+00:00</td><td>approved by local-user</td></tr><tr><td>AWAITING_APPROVAL</td><td>VALIDATING</td><td class=\"mono loc\">2026-10-20T20:45:46.945268Z</td><td>validation requested</td></tr><tr><td>VALIDATING</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td class=\"mono loc\">2026-10-20T20:45:51.715516Z</td><td>PASSED: 8/8 required checks passed</td></tr><tr><td>VALIDATED</td><td>BENCHMARKING</td><td class=\"mono loc\">2026-10-20T20:45:52.256987Z</td><td>benchmark requested</td></tr><tr><td>BENCHMARKING</td><td>COMPLETED</td><td class=\"mono loc\">2026-10-20T20:45:56.487652Z</td><td>benchmark 7e4f1fba-f30a-4243-a54d-68bd3e1f0976: IMPROVED</td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s8\"><span class=\"secnum\">8</span> Correctness validation</h2>\n<p><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> <span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span> PASSED: 8/8 required checks passed <span class=\"muted\">(3.4 s)</span></p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Required checks: isolation, compile, functional_tests, output_equivalence, edge_cases, exception_parity, input_mutation, patched_code_exercised</p>\n<table class=\"data\">\n  <thead><tr><th width=\"22%\">Check</th><th width=\"10%\">Required</th><th width=\"14%\">Status</th><th width=\"54%\">Detail</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td class=\"mono\">isolation</td><td>yes</td><td><span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span></td><td>only workload.py differs from the original</td></tr>\n    <tr><td class=\"mono\">compile</td><td>yes</td><td><span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span></td><td>compiles</td></tr>\n    <tr><td class=\"mono\">functional_tests</td><td>yes</td><td><span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span></td><td>candidate: 29 test(s) passed</td></tr>\n    <tr><td class=\"mono\">output_equivalence</td><td>yes</td><td><span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span></td><td>6 case(s): 6 PASSED, 0 FAILED, 0 INCONCLUSIVE, 0 NOT_RUN</td></tr>\n    <tr><td class=\"mono\">edge_cases</td><td>yes</td><td><span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span></td><td>5 case(s): 5 PASSED, 0 FAILED, 0 INCONCLUSIVE, 0 NOT_RUN</td></tr>\n    <tr><td class=\"mono\">exception_parity</td><td>yes</td><td><span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span></td><td>2 error input(s), 0 not at parity</td></tr>\n    <tr><td class=\"mono\">input_mutation</td><td>yes</td><td><span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span></td><td>no new input mutation across 13 case(s)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td class=\"mono\">patched_code_exercised</td><td>yes</td><td><span class=\"badge status status-passed\">PASSED</span></td><td>tests called `count_duplicates` 14 time(s)</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"muted\">Validated baseline input hashes: <span class=\"mono\">fixture:small:seed=2024</span>=2079162d2fcc\u2026, <span class=\"mono\">fixture:small:seed=7</span>=feb63290f408\u2026, <span class=\"mono\">fixture:small:seed=11</span>=23fd40584a37\u2026, <span class=\"mono\">fixture:medium:seed=2024</span>=f19793195965\u2026, <span class=\"mono\">fixture:medium:seed=7</span>=c1ca3dbc5609\u2026, <span class=\"mono\">fixture:medium:seed=11</span>=7a5f264fd2b7\u2026</p></section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s9\"><span class=\"secnum\">9</span> Benchmark results</h2>\n<p><span class=\"badge prov prov-measured\">MEASURED</span> Benchmark <span class=\"mono\">7e4f1fba-f30a-4243-a54d-68bd3e1f0976</span> \u00b7 <span class=\"badge status status-succeeded\">SUCCEEDED</span> \u00b7 baseline (original) vs validated patch candidate 0042598d-9a45-4f93-81dc-28ddbbbf6504 (deterministic: list_count_to_counter)</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Settings: size small \u00b7 2 warmup(s) \u00b7 8 timed runs per variant (1 call per fresh process) \u00b7 1 memory runs \u00b7 order random \u00b7 seed 12345 \u00b7 10000 bootstrap resamples \u00b7 practical threshold 5.0%</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Input SHA-256 <span class=\"mono\">2079162d2fcc3377eb667681ca4b1ecb92a1ac116a8039c36077954465f05827</span> \u00b7 baseline tree <span class=\"mono\">ebc38e0a5ea566a0</span> \u00b7 candidate tree <span class=\"mono\">1d8241c1da508fbb</span></p>\n<table class=\"kpis\">\n  <tr>\n    <td><span class=\"kpi\">33.13\u00d7</span><br><span class=\"kpi-label\">median speedup</span></td>\n    <td><span class=\"kpi\">30.13\u00d7 \u2013 34.93\u00d7</span><br><span class=\"kpi-label\">95% bootstrap CI</span></td>\n    <td><span class=\"kpi\">97.0%</span><br><span class=\"kpi-label\">latency reduction</span></td>\n    <td><span class=\"kpi\">33.13\u00d7</span><br><span class=\"kpi-label\">throughput speedup</span></td>\n    <td><span class=\"kpi\"><span class=\"badge status status-improved\">IMPROVED</span></span><br><span class=\"kpi-label\">classification</span></td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n<p>CPU-time speedup: 34.25\u00d7</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Classification: speedup 33.132x &gt;= 1.053x (5% threshold) and 95% CI [30.134x, 34.929x] excludes 1 (IMPROVED needs speedup >= 1.053\u00d7 and a CI excluding 1; REGRESSED <= 0.952\u00d7). CI method: paired percentile bootstrap of the ratio of medians.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"760\" height=\"204\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 204\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Benchmark samples\"><title>Raw wall-time samples per variant (MEASURED, ms, log scale)</title><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"760\" height=\"204\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/><g font-family=\"Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#334155\"><line x1=\"292.8\" y1=\"16\" x2=\"292.8\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#e2e8f0\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"292.8\" y=\"184\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.1</text><line x1=\"637.7\" y1=\"16\" x2=\"637.7\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#e2e8f0\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"637.7\" y=\"184\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"730\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/><text x=\"425.0\" y=\"199\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wall time per call (ms, log scale)</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"55.0\" font-weight=\"bold\">baseline</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"69.0\">n=8</text><line x1=\"685.7\" y1=\"59.0\" x2=\"696.6\" y2=\"59.0\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"685.7\" y1=\"51.0\" x2=\"685.7\" y2=\"67.0\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"696.6\" y1=\"51.0\" x2=\"696.6\" y2=\"67.0\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"686.5\" y=\"45.0\" width=\"2.4\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\"0.18\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"686.9\" y1=\"45.0\" x2=\"686.9\" y2=\"73.0\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"685.7\" cy=\"48.0\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"696.6\" cy=\"56.8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"686.6\" cy=\"65.6\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"687.1\" cy=\"50.2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"689.8\" cy=\"59.0\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"686.0\" cy=\"67.8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"688.5\" cy=\"52.4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"686.7\" cy=\"61.2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#64748b\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><text x=\"686.9\" y=\"41.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">median 1.38879 ms</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"129.0\" font-weight=\"bold\">candidate</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"143.0\">n=8</text><line x1=\"153.4\" y1=\"133.0\" x2=\"179.6\" y2=\"133.0\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"153.4\" y1=\"125.0\" x2=\"153.4\" y2=\"141.0\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"179.6\" y1=\"125.0\" x2=\"179.6\" y2=\"141.0\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"159.0\" y=\"119.0\" width=\"9.9\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\"0.18\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"162.5\" y1=\"119.0\" x2=\"162.5\" y2=\"147.0\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"153.4\" cy=\"122.0\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"162.0\" cy=\"130.8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"165.1\" cy=\"139.6\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"160.5\" cy=\"124.2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"179.5\" cy=\"133.0\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"179.6\" cy=\"141.8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"154.2\" cy=\"126.4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><circle cx=\"162.9\" cy=\"135.2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2563eb\" fill-opacity=\"0.75\"/><text x=\"162.5\" y=\"115.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">median 0.0419 ms</text></g></svg><p class=\"caption\">Figure 1. Raw wall-time samples per variant (MEASURED): box = interquartile range, thick line = median, whiskers = min\u2013max, dots = individual timed runs.</p></div><h3>Per-variant statistics</h3>\n<table class=\"data\">\n  <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Metric</th><th class=\"num\">n</th><th class=\"num\">Median</th><th class=\"num\">Mean</th><th class=\"num\">Min</th><th class=\"num\">Max</th><th class=\"num\">Stdev</th><th class=\"num\">p95</th><th class=\"num\">CV</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>baseline</td><td>wall</td><td class=\"num\">8</td><td class=\"num\">1.389 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.403 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.377 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.481 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.034 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.458 ms</td><td class=\"num\">2.4%</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>baseline</td><td>CPU</td><td class=\"num\">8</td><td class=\"num\">1.387 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.394 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.373 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.441 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.023 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.431 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.6%</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>candidate</td><td>wall</td><td class=\"num\">8</td><td class=\"num\">0.042 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.043 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.039 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.047 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.003 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.047 ms</td><td class=\"num\">6.8%</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>candidate</td><td>CPU</td><td class=\"num\">8</td><td class=\"num\">0.041 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.041 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.038 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.045 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.002 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.044 ms</td><td class=\"num\">5.6%</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"warning\">Small sample: p95 estimated from only n=8 samples is unstable (it depends on the 1 slowest run(s))</p><h3>Memory comparison</h3>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 baseline / 1 candidate memory run(s), separate from the timed runs. tracemalloc and RSS are different quantities and are not compared with each other.</p>\n<table class=\"data\">\n  <thead><tr><th width=\"26%\">Metric</th><th width=\"13%\" class=\"num\">Baseline (median)</th><th width=\"13%\" class=\"num\">Candidate (median)</th><th width=\"10%\" class=\"num\">Ratio</th><th width=\"38%\">Definition</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody><tr><td>tracemalloc peak (Python allocations, call only)</td><td class=\"num\">2.5 KiB</td><td class=\"num\">9.2 KiB</td><td class=\"num\">3.73\u00d7</td><td>peak Python-traced allocations during the workload call only (input built before tracing); not process memory</td></tr><tr><td>RSS peak (sampled, whole child process)</td><td class=\"num\">26.3 MiB</td><td class=\"num\">25.9 MiB</td><td class=\"num\">0.98\u00d7</td><td>peak resident set size of the child process, sampled by the parent every 5 ms over the whole process lifetime (interpreter + input + call); short spikes between samples can be missed</td></tr><tr><td>ru_maxrss (kernel max RSS, whole child process)</td><td class=\"num\">26.7 MiB</td><td class=\"num\">26.2 MiB</td><td class=\"num\">0.98\u00d7</td><td>kernel-reported maximum RSS of the child process (getrusage)</td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\n<p class=\"muted\">Output check during the benchmark: equivalent=True, comparison=exact, detail=outputs are identical</p><ul class=\"muted\"><li>speedup = median_baseline / median_candidate (wall time)</li><li>latency_reduction_percent = (median_baseline - median_candidate) / median_baseline * 100</li><li>throughput_speedup = candidate_throughput / baseline_throughput</li></ul><h3>Warnings and noise</h3>\n<p class=\"warning\">p95 estimated from only n=8 samples is unstable (it depends on the 1 slowest run(s))</p><h3>Raw timing samples</h3>\n<p class=\"muted\">20 sample rows (16 timed); every row is in the CSV export.</p>\n<table class=\"data\">\n  <thead><tr><th class=\"num\">Pair</th><th>Variant</th><th class=\"num\">Position</th><th class=\"num\">Wall</th><th class=\"num\">CPU</th><th>OK</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody><tr><td class=\"num\">0</td><td>baseline</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">1.377 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.373 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">0</td><td>candidate</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">0.039 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.038 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">1</td><td>candidate</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">0.042 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.040 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">1</td><td>baseline</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">1.481 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.441 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">2</td><td>baseline</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">1.386 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.382 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">2</td><td>candidate</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">0.043 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.041 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">3</td><td>baseline</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">1.391 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.389 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">3</td><td>candidate</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">0.041 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.040 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">4</td><td>candidate</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">0.047 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.042 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">4</td><td>baseline</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">1.415 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.412 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">5</td><td>baseline</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">1.380 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.373 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">5</td><td>candidate</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">0.047 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.045 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">6</td><td>baseline</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">1.403 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.399 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">6</td><td>candidate</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">0.040 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.038 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">7</td><td>candidate</td><td class=\"num\">0</td><td class=\"num\">0.042 ms</td><td class=\"num\">0.041 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">7</td><td>baseline</td><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"num\">1.387 ms</td><td class=\"num\">1.385 ms</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s10\"><span class=\"secnum\">10</span> Reproducibility</h2>\n<p>Command line:</p>\n<div class=\"commands\"><div class=\"dl ctx\">.venv/bin/python scripts/optimize_workload.py duplicate_counter --approve --profile-size small --recommendation 1 --size small --warmups 2 --runs 8 --memory-runs 1 --threshold 5 --seed 12345</div></div>\n<p>HTTP API (relative to the PerfPilot base URL):</p>\n<div class=\"commands\"><div class=\"dl ctx\">POST /api/profiles {&#34;workload_id&#34;: &#34;7d86df69-0a5d-4393-840e-b2ef507a89b6&#34;, &#34;size&#34;: &#34;small&#34;}</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">POST /api/analyses {&#34;workload_id&#34;: &#34;7d86df69-0a5d-4393-840e-b2ef507a89b6&#34;, &#34;profile_id&#34;: &#34;d9eb8786-9e05-4ee6-b1b3-dc5c2e1511a3&#34;}</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">GET /api/analyses/bd27864a-8771-443f-924c-262d57fb2ca5/recommendations</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">POST /api/optimizations {&#34;recommendation_id&#34;: &#34;535fbab1-5007-4fe8-986e-f6c059099111&#34;}</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">GET /api/optimizations/0042598d-9a45-4f93-81dc-28ddbbbf6504/diff</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">POST /api/optimizations/0042598d-9a45-4f93-81dc-28ddbbbf6504/approve {&#34;approved_by&#34;: &#34;local-user&#34;}</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">POST /api/optimizations/0042598d-9a45-4f93-81dc-28ddbbbf6504/validate</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">GET /api/optimizations/0042598d-9a45-4f93-81dc-28ddbbbf6504/validation</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">POST /api/benchmarks {&#34;workload_id&#34;: &#34;7d86df69-0a5d-4393-840e-b2ef507a89b6&#34;, &#34;candidate&#34;: {&#34;candidate_id&#34;: &#34;0042598d-9a45-4f93-81dc-28ddbbbf6504&#34;}, &#34;size&#34;: &#34;small&#34;, &#34;warmups&#34;: 2, &#34;runs&#34;: 8, &#34;memory_runs&#34;: 1, &#34;threshold_percent&#34;: 5.0, &#34;seed&#34;: 12345, &#34;order&#34;: &#34;random&#34;, &#34;bootstrap_resamples&#34;: 10000}</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">GET /api/benchmarks/7e4f1fba-f30a-4243-a54d-68bd3e1f0976/results</div><div class=\"dl ctx\">POST /api/optimizations/0042598d-9a45-4f93-81dc-28ddbbbf6504/reports {&#34;formats&#34;: [&#34;md&#34;, &#34;json&#34;, &#34;html&#34;, &#34;csv&#34;, &#34;pdf&#34;]}</div></div>\n<ul class=\"muted\"><li>The IDs are those of this experiment; re-running the steps creates new records (the bundled workload source is unchanged, see the tree hashes).</li><li>Every POST that starts work returns 202 and a job id; poll GET /api/jobs/{job_id}.</li></ul></section>\n\n<section>\n<h2 id=\"s11\"><span class=\"secnum\">11</span> Limitations</h2>\n<ul><li>Bundled workloads run on the host in constrained child processes (fresh interpreter, scrubbed environment, rlimits, timeouts), not on dedicated benchmark hardware; read the warnings and the environment fingerprint before trusting small differences.</li><li>Correctness validation covers only the tests and inputs it exercised. It is evidence of equivalence, not a proof.</li><li>tracemalloc (Python-traced allocations during the call) and RSS (sampled process memory) measure different things and are never compared with each other.</li><li>cProfile times are inflated by instrumentation: the profile shows where time goes, the benchmark shows how fast the code runs.</li><li>Only 8 timed runs per variant: p95 and the bootstrap CI are unstable at this sample size; re-run with more runs on a quiet machine to confirm.</li></ul>\n</section>\n\n<footer class=\"report-footer\">\n  <p>Generated by PerfPilot AI 0.1.0 on 2026-10-20 20:45 UTC \u00b7 optimization <span class=\"mono\">0042598d-9a45-4f93-81dc-28ddbbbf6504</span> \u00b7 experiment schema 1.0 \u00b7 0 secret-like values redacted.</p>\n</footer>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
